Based on the discussion in the previous sections we propose the following: Proposal 1 RAN2 to adopt Option B as the Rel-19 baseline: → Boundary for CBRA failure detection = reception of the next R2D trigger message or subsequent paging message. → Keep Option C as an optional enhancement for future releases (e.g., Rel-20) where dense deployments or high-collision environments may require additional reader flexibility. Proposal 2 RAN2 to define Frequency Index as an optional field in Msg2: → Presence of Frequency Index indicated by a presence bit. → Reader includes Frequency Index only when collision risk is high (e.g., dense deployments or high load). → Default behavior in low-density scenarios is to omit the field to save overhead.

